SUMMARY
New table public.depreciation_reports, PK (property_id,
financial_year_end). Columns: div43_annual, div40_annual (both >= 0),
storage_path, qs_firm, report_date, notes, timestamps.

FILES
- supabase/migrations/056_depreciation_reports.sql (new)
- lib/supabase/database.types.ts - DepreciationReport row type + Tables
  entry

DESIGN DECISION: RECORD, DO NOT DERIVE
Div 40 depends on per-asset effective lives, prime cost vs diminishing
value, and the post-9-May-2017 restriction on previously-used plant in
second-hand residential property. A QS already determines this and issues
a schedule. Deriving it here would duplicate paid work and take on
liability that conflicts with "decision support, never automated filing"
in conductor/product.md. The table stores the surveyor's stated annual
figures and keeps the report as evidence.

One row per property per FY. The same PDF normally covers several years,
so storage_path repeating across rows is intended, not a duplicate -
explicitly verified as permitted.

